# Normalise line endings in the repository, and let the working copy follow the platform.
* text=auto

# The vendored artifacts are the exception, and the reason is the point of vendoring them: each is
# pinned by SHA-256 in its PROVENANCE.md and checked by tests/test_vendored_artifacts.py. With
# `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for Windows default — a checkout would rewrite every LF in the
# schemas into CRLF, so a fresh clone would hold files whose bytes no longer match the digests that
# attest to what was downloaded from the Ministry. The test would be red on a clean checkout, and
# the honest reading of that failure would be wrong: nothing was substituted, only re-encoded.
schemas/*.xsd -text
src/doc_extract/assets/fonts/** -text

# Rendered corpora are written as bytes for the same reason (see synth/corpus.py), and are not
# committed — this covers the case of someone unignoring them locally.
*.pdf -text
*.xml -text
